# Security headers, added 19-08-2026 after the deploy preview #9 audit
# embedded the entire live site in a cross-origin iframe and it worked.
#
# This lives in public/_headers rather than in a netlify.toml on purpose.
# netlify.toml is read relative to the build's base directory, and the site
# root is the rkade-website/ subfolder of this repo, so a toml at either
# level is a guess about how the Netlify site is configured. Everything in
# public/ is copied into dist/ verbatim by the build, so _headers is correct
# no matter what the base directory turns out to be.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here yet. Getting one wrong silently breaks the
# page rather than failing loudly, and it needs its own test pass against a
# preview before it goes anywhere near the live site.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
